update Sipho (Warm)
Sipho: Did you know a corrugated roof sheds nearly all of what lands on it? Almost none soaks in, not like thatch.
- So?
	Hope: So?
	Sipho: So every roof in this village is a catchment surface we're just letting run into the dirt.
	Sipho: Four metres by six is twenty-four square metres. One decent storm on that is — a lot. More than a drum holds, anyway. Which is the problem.
	Sipho: Anyway. It's not complicated. That's what bothers me about it.
